# tests/assertions/view_edge.rxt -- [OPT-VEDGE] the view-tolerant scan edge.
#
# Counted single-class chains under a `\z`/`\Z`/`$` position view: the forward
# and anchored machines' END-view-only members (scanedge.c precondition (3)
# relaxed) and the reverse machine's chain whose head is its start state's
# view target (precondition (6) trimmed). Subjects straddle the count bound,
# end on a non-class byte, carry a trailing newline, and every start position
# is searched (`ms`), so each scan exit (bound reached, run stopped inside,
# run stopped at n) is reached from each entry. -fno-view-edge is the
# reference: the same cells must hold under it (test-axes).
#
# Expectations oracle-verified against python3 `re` (`search(s, pos)`; PCRE
# `\z` -> `\Z`, PCRE `\Z` -> `(?=\n?\Z)`, `$` unchanged), generated 2026-10-03.

pattern (?:[a-z]{0,4})\z
features assertions
